    {
      "id": "docs_specs_2026_07_31_coding_standards_drizzle_bypasses_rls",
      "label": "Drizzle / postgres.js bypasses RLS",
      "file_type": "rationale",
      "source_file": "docs/specs/2026-07-31-coding-standards.md",
      "source_location": "L57",
      "source_url": null,
      "captured_at": null,
      "author": null,
      "contributor": null,
      "rationale": "A direct pooler connection runs as the table owner, so tenancy must be scoped in WHERE clauses or via SET LOCAL request.jwt.claims + SET ROLE authenticated; decide before multi-tenancy ships."
    },
    {
      "id": "docs_specs_2026_07_31_coding_standards_strict_csp",
      "label": "Strict nonce + strict-dynamic CSP",
      "file_type": "rationale",
      "source_file": "docs/specs/2026-07-31-coding-standards.md",
      "source_location": "L69",
      "source_url": null,
      "captured_at": null,
      "author": null,
      "contributor": null,
      "rationale": "A nonce CSP forces dynamic rendering, and @supabase/ssr cookies are not HttpOnly by design, so the strict script-src CSP is the primary defense against session-token theft. style-src 'unsafe-inline' is an accepted trade-off for Radix/shadcn inline styles."
    },
